# The app's own ignores, kept here rather than in the repository root.
#
# The root .gitignore anchors `/node_modules` to the repository root, so it
# does not cover this directory. Keeping the app's ignores local means the
# webapp's ignore file does not have to grow a mobile section, and the two
# stay independent — which is the same reason `mobile/` is inert to the VPS
# deploy (ADR-0002).

node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/

# expo prebuild output. This project stays managed (continuous native
# generation): app.json is the single source of native config, and the Kotlin
# module in mobile/modules/ autolinks without a committed native project.
# A committed android/ would become a second, silently diverging source.
/android
/ios

*.log
npm-debug.*
.DS_Store

# Signing material and service accounts never belong in git, on any branch.
*.jks
*.keystore
google-services.json
credentials.json
